\@writefile{lox}{\contentsline {fixme}{\color  {fxerror}Actually, the above needs much more fleshing out due to the annoyance of the need to use the AC-reductions on matches to get termination in the presence of cycles, which requires another use of Dickson's lemma. Of course this is again highlighting the connection between matching and closure, but it needs probably at least a whole section}{31}{subsection.4.4.3}\protected@file@percent }
